      "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe LoRA merge cache bails out on any multi-rank run:\n\n```python\nif dist.is_initialized() and dist.get_world_size() > 1:\n    # Sharded weights would need per-rank stores; not worth it until a\n    # multi-GPU consumer deployment exists.\n    return None\n```\n\nThe reason holds for a tensor- or FSDP-sharded replica: each rank holds a different slice, so one entry per module name would be wrong for all but one of them. It does not hold for sequence- and data-parallel replicas, whose ranks hold the same full weights — those ranks can share one entry, and the cache is what keeps 62 GiB of merged weights out of anonymous host memory per rank.\n\n## Modifications\n\nDecide on the sharding that actually changes the local weights — `tp_size > 1` or `use_fsdp_inference` — instead of on the world size. Every rank then merges through the same entry: each file is written via `tmp.<pid>` + rename, so concurrent writers produce the same bytes and one manifest wins.\n\nNothing changes for a single-rank run, and the sharded cases still fall back to per-rank in-place merges.\n\n## Tests\n\n`test_merge_cache_serves_replicated_replicas_only` — the cache is offered at `tp_size=1`/no FSDP and refused at `tp_size=2` and at `use_fsdp_inference=True`. `python/sglang/multimodal_gen/test/unit/test_lora_pipeline.py` passes (21 tests).\n\nMeasured on a 2-card H3 engine with a 780 MB adapter: the engine adopted the existing cache instead of merging (`LoRA merge cache found for transformer; adopting instead of merging`), load dropped from 230 s to 170 s, the layerwise pin budget recovered from 147 GiB to 398 GiB, and the engine's two ranks held 150 GiB Pss together instead of 254 GiB.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39752805709](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39752805709)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39752805693](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39752805693)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39752805729](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39752805729)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
